    "checks/independent/dfm-continuum-refinement-limit.py": {
      "role": "Bounded exact dyadic-cell transport verification application with an owned word value object, checked scalar/permutation callbacks, Railway operations and factored geometric/covariance controls",
      "origin": "lean4/DressingFieldRefinementLimit.lean",
      "profile": "Exact",
      "cost": "Input words<=64 bool bits; depth0..12 and total word length<=64. Refinement creates<=4096 immutable words, O(2^depth*(word_length+depth)) work/storage. Scalar/ordered transport invoke a trusted synchronous callback once per leaf, at most4096 times; callback execution cost is external to this bound. Exact scalar edges and every accumulation have<=4096-bit numerator/denominator; S3 operations use exactly three integer labels. Fixed fixture words have length<=3, scalar depths<=9, S3 depths<=6. Default14642 obligations =14336 scalar+306 noncommutative; no convergence search is performed.",
      "groups": [
        {
          "requirement": "Own a little-endian bool word of at most64 bits, compute exact rational endpoints, and enumerate its binary descendants in increasing interval order. Preflight exact depth0..12 and combined64-bit length before allocating leaves. Return Outcome from refinement and preserve the legacy detached list-of-tuples export.",
